From 273a1f8f7eb0c840491990b903c2ad8e3c8eaa8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 11:28:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06897/11362] [outer-loop] lf52: L6 SOLVED round 6 (recovered
 from timed-out session)

Round-6 gpt-5.6-sol session found a genuine L6 win live at session step
615 (312-action banked L5-verified prefix + a 303-action L6 route), but
was then killed by its 40-minute wall-clock timeout while continuing
into L7 exploration rather than stopping to gate the win -- it never
wrote a result artifact.

Recovered the raw action sequence from the process's own saved
candidate file (/tmp/lf52_candidate.json, written via the session's own
'save' REPL command), reconstructed a proper result artifact at
results/outer_loop_fable5_lf52_probe_l6_20260712.json from the
recovered sequence plus narrative/gotchas quoted from the session
transcript, added a new >=6 priority branch to resolve_replay_plan(),
and independently verified via the actual resolver + 5x fresh
env.reset() + replay: all 5 trials confirmed level=6,
state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED (more levels remain beyond 6; L7 was
reached but not explored).

Key L6 mechanics: a color-8 quad block that jumps over pegs WITHOUT
removing them (movable, indestructible obstacle, not a second peg
type); a double-socket carrier that reveals a second hidden chamber
after seven eastward rail moves (L6 is multi-screen, unlike
single-screen L5); an in-level keyhole reset that preserves the banked
L5 prefix.

ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml: lf52 levels_reproduced 5 -> 6.
reproducible_total_levels 158 -> 159 (sum-checked;
arc_count_integrity_lint exit 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
